  "orgStructureNoSqlId": "78741291-51fd-41d3-a7f2-032e2e23d4d0",
  "description": "<p>St. Olaf students are invited to register to attend the <a href=\"https://wp.stolaf.edu/taylorcenter/files/2026/08/2026-PowWow-Trip-Poster-3.jpg\" target=\"\">54th Annual Traditional Mahkato Wacipi (Pow Wow) Trip to Mankato, MN.</a> </p><p>This trip organized by the Taylor Center is an opportunity for all students to learn about Dakota Culture in Minnesota. </p><p></p><h4 style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><a href=\"https://forms.gle/iNPp769mLDTNicN6A\" target=\"\">RSVP HERE!</a></u></h4><h4 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><b>Trip Details:</b></span></h4><ul><li>Free transportation and entrance ticket to registered participants is provided. </li><li>Food is available for purchase from vendors in-site. </li><li>Departure from Buntrock Commons: 11:45 a.m. | Return from event: 3:00 p.m.</li><li>Location: Dakota Wokiksuye Makoce (Land of Memories Park), Mankato, Minnesota.</li><li>All attendees are expected to follow the <a href=\"https://www.mahkatowacipi.org/for-visitors\">Guidelines for Visitors</a> from <span style=\"color: black;\">The Mahkato Mdewakanton Association.</span></li></ul>",
